# SPURIOUS_DATA records with Type Word bit 14 (the error flag) set: labelled
# SPURIOUS, not ERROR -- the message type decides the label, as it decides the
# 0x2000/0x2001 code and the timing (docs/DATAFLOW.md row S7).

# Errored RT15 SA11 Receive with one captured payload word and DDC error 0x011E.
02470F1826DB21F6
7E79 0004 1E01

# SPURIOUS_DATA continuation (0x2000) with two raw words; Type Word 0x4620 has
# bit 14 set.
20460F1826DB38F7
AAAA BBBB

# Normal record clears the continuation flag.
04240F1826DBE3F9
DE7E 0078
2010 8241 0000 0815 0000 0000 0000 0000
00FE 0000 0000 0000 0000 0000 0000 0000
0000 0000 0300 0000 0000 0000 0000 0000
0000 0020 0000 0000 0000 0000

# Standalone SPURIOUS_DATA (0x2001), also with bit 14 set.
20460F1826DBE3FA
CCCC DDDD
